description:
Dragging a row of a reorderable list onto another row moves it there. Write

```cpp
template <typename T>
void moveItem(std::vector<T>& items, int from, int to);
```

Take the item at `from` out and insert it so that it ends up at index `to` (counted in the final list). Indexes outside the list, or `from == to`, change nothing.

```
{ A, B, C, D, E }, from 1 to 3  ->  { A, C, D, B, E }
{ A, B, C, D, E }, from 4 to 0  ->  { E, A, B, C, D }
```

